From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luna <luna@localhost>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 09:10:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] x86: move Luna boot handoff parser to Rust

Make the Luna-specific kernel boot handoff logic Rust-first.

The C side remains only as a tiny ABI bridge from setup_arch() into the
Rust implementation. The parser itself validates Linux setup_data,
LunaBootHandoffV1 framing, and the required LUNA_INIT_IMAGE record.

This keeps the early boot call site intact while making the Luna-specific
logic use the kernel Rust infrastructure.

---
 arch/x86/kernel/Makefile     |   1 +
 arch/x86/kernel/luna_boot.rs | 266 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 arch/x86/kernel/setup.c      |   2 +
 include/linux/luna_boot.h    |  25 +++++
 4 files changed, 294 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/x86/kernel/luna_boot.rs
 create mode 100644 include/linux/luna_boot.h

diff --git a/arch/x86/kernel/Makefile b/arch/x86/kernel/Makefile
--- a/arch/x86/kernel/Makefile
+++ b/arch/x86/kernel/Makefile
@@ -1,1 +1,2 @@
+@@ -1,1 +1,2 @@
